{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Ibn Majah","section":{"25":{"eng-name":"Chapters on Hajj Rituals","ara-name":"كتاب المناسك"}},"section_detail":{"25":{"hadithnumber_first":2882,"hadithnumber_last":3119,"arabicnumber_first":2882,"arabicnumber_last":3119}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":2988,"arabicnumber":2988,"text":"Rapporté par Ibn ‘Umar : Si je vais vite entre Safa et Marwah, c’est parce que j’ai vu le Messager d’Allah (ﷺ) aller vite, et si je marche, c’est parce que je l’ai vu marcher, même si je suis un vieil homme","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Hasan"}],"reference":{"book":25,"hadith":107},"chapter":{"id":43,"ara-name":"باب السَّعْىِ بَيْنَ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةِ","eng-name":"Sa`y between Safa and Marwah","isFirstHadith":false}}]}